{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim","id":768872,"title":"[Ex3] Some questions on Aim","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T19:28:58-08:00","id":768872,"title":"[Ex3] Some questions on Aim","content":"* Can you perform multiple Aim Actions in a row to stack the bonus? Ahlat's Horizon-Breaker Shot seems to sort of assume you can?<br /> * If you can perform an Aim Action reflexively (like Righteous Devil Form), does the bonus apply to this turn or the next one?<br /> * If you can perform multiple Aim Actions in the same turn (i.e. Cloud of Ebon Devils + Righteous Devil Form), does their bonus stack?<br /> * If you you are benefiting from an Aim Action while you use a charm that creates extra attacks (i.e. Trance of Unhesitating Speed) do the bonuses apply to every attack roll in the action, or just one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 11-18-2015, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:11:37-08:00","id":768904,"title":"","content":"Hm... My opinions on this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim#post768872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Can you perform multiple Aim Actions in a row to stack the bonus? Ahlat's Horizon-Breaker Shot seems to sort of assume you can?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that multiple aim actions normally can't apply more that +3 dice to one attack, and would only spend more turns aiming to hit at Medium range or greater, or for Charm effects.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you can perform an Aim Action reflexively (like Righteous Devil Form), does the bonus apply to this turn or the next one? </div> </div> </div>The same turn, if you aim reflexively before making the attack.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you can perform multiple Aim Actions in the same turn (i.e. Cloud of Ebon Devils + Righteous Devil Form), does their bonus stack? </div> </div> </div>I don't think you can get two Reflexive aims out of CoED and RDF. The reflexive aim of CoED only applies when you roll Join Battle with it, and reflexively entering RDF requires you to hit someone with a Decisive Attack.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you you are benefiting from an Aim Action while you use a charm that creates extra attacks (i.e. Trance of Unhesitating Speed) do the bonuses apply to every attack roll in the action, or just one? </div> </div> </div>I would say... Every attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T20:49:49-08:00","id":768922,"title":"","content":"Re: &quot;I don't think you can get two Reflexive aims out of CoED and RDF. The reflexive aim of CoED only applies when you roll Join Battle with it, and reflexively entering RDF requires you to hit someone with a Decisive Attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> You use your reflexive to aim and your normal action to aim for a total of two aims. You actually *can* get a third if you get Accuracy Without Distance and make an Archery Attack (not a Martial Arts attack).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:06:59-08:00","id":768929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=768922#post768922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: &quot;I don't think you can get two Reflexive aims out of CoED and RDF. The reflexive aim of CoED only applies when you roll Join Battle with it, and reflexively entering RDF requires you to hit someone with a Decisive Attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> You use your reflexive to aim and your normal action to aim for a total of two aims. You actually *can* get a third if you get Accuracy Without Distance and make an Archery Attack (not a Martial Arts attack).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno if you can combo CoED with an Archery charm, since it's a Supplemental charm and I'm pretty sure you can't combine Supplemental charms of different abilities.<br /> <br /> But alright, you get two Aim Actions using CoED and your normal action to Aim again. On your next turn, you can probably use Blossom of Inevitable Demise to attack someone out to Medium range with the +3 bonus dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T21:28:11-08:00","id":768940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim#post768872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Can you perform multiple Aim Actions in a row to stack the bonus? Ahlat's Horizon-Breaker Shot seems to sort of assume you can?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the Aim action normally only grants the +3 bonus if you attack on the following turn. Multiple Aim actions over multiple turns can be taken for other reasons (range, the Horizon-Breaker Shot, etc.) but unless you declare on attack on that target on your <i>next turn </i>you get no bonus. As long as you are performing only one Aim action per turn, only the most recent one is going to count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you can perform an Aim Action reflexively (like Righteous Devil Form), does the bonus apply to this turn or the next one? </div> </div> </div>Here's where plain text starts to break down a little, since the book clearly states &quot;Should his character attack that target on his <i>next </i>turn, the attack gains a +3 bonus&quot; (emphasis mine). The intent of allowing an Aim action to be completed immediately seems plain, though. You should get the bonus on the attack that immediately follows the Aim action, so long as it occurs at the next opportunity. It would be pretty odd if you didn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you can perform multiple Aim Actions in the same turn (i.e. Cloud of Ebon Devils + Righteous Devil Form), does their bonus stack? </div> </div> </div>The book appears to be silent on this, as far as I can tell, presumably since without using magic to complete an Aim action reflexively it would be impossible to do. However, CoED won't allow you to do this anyway. You could use CoED to get a free Aim action as part of your Join Battle roll and then use your combat action to Aim as well, but...then you have given up your combat action on your &quot;next turn&quot; (your opportunity to <i>use </i>the bonus from the Aim action that CoED gave you) in favor of performing a second Aim action. They won't stack because you had your chance to use the first Aim bonus and didn't, and now that window has passed.<br /> <br /> Using AWD on top of the Reflexive Aim from CoED is harder to answer. By a rigid reading of RAW it looks like you could do this. The question of whether the bonuses stack, then, seems to default to ST judgment. I can't find anything one way or another. FWIW I would say no, but I freely admit this is based on absolutely nothing other than my own preference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> * If you you are benefiting from an Aim Action while you use a charm that creates extra attacks (i.e. Trance of Unhesitating Speed) do the bonuses apply to every attack roll in the action, or just one? </div> </div> </div>It says &quot;the attack&quot; so this is open to interpretation. So long as the attack action <i>only </i>targets the person you Aimed at, I would rule that it applied to every roll that was a part of that action. But I could see the argument against as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T22:10:51-08:00","id":768965,"title":"","content":"RDF is what allows for two aim actions, not CoED.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T10:20:27-08:00","id":769373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=768965#post768965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RDF is what allows for two aim actions, not CoED.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either/or, really (read the Mastery effect of CoED again). You could make the case that the reflexive Aim action of RDF one is a stickier wicket, but this is just arguing over details for the sake of it. The real problem is that the book doesn't directly address whether or not multiple Aim actions stack, likely because under normal circumstances they can't (or, to be more precise, they <i>won't </i>because of timing). When you use magic to <i>make </i>it happen, the rules are silent and it is up to the ST to adjudicate what happens.<br /> <br /> My own ruling would be that you can leverage multiple instant Aim actions to, say, make an attack from Long range immediately, or to benefit effects like the Horizon-Breaker, but I wouldn't allow more than one +3 bonus to apply. Again, there is absolutely no solid basis for this. It's just what I would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:06:34-08:00","id":769410,"title":"","content":"So here's my question about Aim: why can't it be placed in a flurry, not even with social actions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:13:59-08:00","id":769419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=769410#post769410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's my question about Aim: why can't it be placed in a flurry, not even with social actions?</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be able to flurry with socials, yes, but the intent was to make sure that the Archer/Thrown character cannot stay at long range forever by Aim+Attacking at long range, then moving backwards, rinse and repeat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T11:17:22-08:00","id":769421,"title":"","content":"Literal, pedantic answer? Because the rules say it can't.<br /> <br /> Justification for that rule? I'd imagine it's because Aiming represents specifically blocking out distractions in favor of concentrating on a precise shot. If you're Flurrying, you are by definition <i>not </i>doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T17:15:06-08:00","id":789023,"title":"","content":"Does the &quot;reflexive aim&quot; still count as having taken an <b>aim action</b> for the turn in regards to denying you your <b>movement </b>for the turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/660-souls512","name":"Souls512","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar660_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T07:26:58-08:00","id":789246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Souls512</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=789023#post789023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the &quot;reflexive aim&quot; still count as having taken an <b>aim action</b> for the turn in regards to denying you your <b>movement </b>for the turn?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the whole point of the aim action is to keep ranged fighters from being able to kite forever, I'd say that it does prevent your movement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T23:19:19-08:00","id":789625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=789246#post789246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the whole point of the aim action is to keep ranged fighters from being able to kite forever, I'd say that it does prevent your movement.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 196</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Characters cannot move and aim during the same round without some form of magic to permit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only can do reflexive aim through magic so I would allow it. You could also read it that you need magic for movement though. Since you are burning motes to perform the magic either way it should not unbalance the game.<br /> <br /> Multiple reflexive aim actions could benefit charms like Seven Omens Shot to shorten the long aim action further.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T15:47:51-08:00","id":813711,"title":"","content":"A little bit of thread necromancy, some additional questions about Aim.<br /> <br /> The Aim action cannot be explicitly be placed in furry and the aiming character cannot explicitly move and you have to do Aim action if you want to attack from medium or greater range (without some magic). This rule was introduced to reduce the kitting problem where a ranged attacker could just keep attacking her target while keeping safe distance.<br /> <br /> Now how should we treat a situation where the movement is done by a thirst party and not the archer herself? For example think about trained horses, intelligent familiars, war chariots with drivers, cirrus skiff spell, etc.<br /> On one hand the kitting problem remains on the other hand if you invest in horse or war chariot it should give you some advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T08:53:15-08:00","id":814163,"title":"","content":"Interesting question. Believe it or not I think there is a Ride Charm that may have an answer for us:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seasoned Beast Rider's Approach</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition, when the Solar commands<br /> her mount to perform a Ride-based movement<br /> action, it no longer uses up the Exalt\u2019s movement action<br /> for the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>This requires a little bit of reading between the lines, but seems to indicate that under normal circumstances a character who is mounted must use their own Move action to move, even if it's the horse (or other mount) doing the actual running. That would definitely preclude any Aiming. On the other hand, it also seems to suggest that while using SBRA you <i>could </i>do this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T09:17:12-07:00","id":1515541,"title":"","content":"Hi, this is an old thread but I figured it was a good place. Can you aim precombat to ambush someone from medium range or farther? <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, rules as written, you'd have to spend your first round of combat aiming which would nullify your ambush. This makes almost no sense to the sniper from the bell tower scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T09:03:02-07:00","id":1516012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768872-ex3-some-questions-on-aim?p=1515541#post1515541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, this is an old thread but I figured it was a good place. Can you aim precombat to ambush someone from medium range or farther?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, rules as written, you'd have to spend your first round of combat aiming which would nullify your ambush. This makes almost no sense to the sniper from the bell tower scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. You can't do it.<br /> <br /> The point of combat is a dynamic scene of back-and-forth. The limitation on ranged attacks not sniping someone from a mile away is part of that.<br /> <br /> If you have a situation where one character can delete another character with impunity, that's not a combat scene. If it's a PC in the bell tower, I'd use the &quot;Skip It&quot; sidebar on page 212. If it's an NPC in the tower and I want to kill a character, then I do that by ST fiat.<br /> <br /> If I don't want to kill a PC by sniping them with impunity, I use the RAW. The sniper uses Aim: it's no longer an ambush as the prickles run down the PC's spine, and their eyes furtively dart around for danger as the breath of war quickens them. The sniper makes a Surprise Attack from Medium Range, with whatever other narrative advantages the bell tower grants (like locked doors). The PC can either reflexive move away then Disengage, or do something like this: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/c2k_kuU84ro?t=184\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/c2k_kuU84ro?t=184</a><br /> <br /> (Or you could have a custom Charm or other ability to convert a Surprise Attack into an Ambush or to Aim Reflexively. I'm not your mother.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}